# Accepted vulnerabilities, checked by the image and filesystem scans in
# .github/workflows/{ci,security}.yml.
#
# Both scans already pass --ignore-unfixed, so anything listed here is a CVE
# that DOES have a fix available and is being accepted anyway. That needs a
# reason and an expiry, or the file quietly becomes a way to switch the gate off.
#
# Format — one CVE id per line, each preceded by why and until when:
#
#   # CVE-2024-00000 — <package>. Reachable only from <path>, which this service
#   # never calls. Upstream fix lands in <version>. Re-check: 2026-01-31.
#   CVE-2024-00000
#
# Empty on purpose: nothing is currently being waived.
